  "uncertain": [
    "Left 3-pin ports 1-6: the image draws each port as a separate housing with a horizontal GND/5V/signal label strip but does not show the pin positions inside each port; transcribed as six separate 1-row connectors (could instead be grouped as one 3xN header) and the within-port order is taken from the label strip, not from drawn pins.",
    "5V/GND 2x2 block at bottom left: labeled cells only, no pin numbers or callout; it is not certain this is a wiring header, and the row orientation (vertical 5V/GND columns vs horizontal rows) is inferred."
  ],
  "notes": "Image: LattePanda V1 pinout diagram, Version V1.2 rev1 2017/07/28. The CPU header, TP connector and MIPI-DSI connector carry an 'Operating Voltage 0~1.8V' warning (on TP and MIPI-DSI the warning box encloses the I2C/INT/RESET and MIPI lane pins respectively). TP and MIPI-DSI pins are read from enlarged callouts (their on-board outlines are unlabeled). Skipped per rule 1: Arduino RESET, POWER and RESET buttons; RX0/TX0/D13 LEDs (D17 tag on RX0 LED); USB/Ethernet/HDMI/audio/microSD connectors without individual pin labels. Arduino header label = D-name, other printed names (A-number, PWM, RXD1/TXD1, SDA/SCL, D13 LED) as functions read outward from the pin."
}